---
---

<section id="nearby-food" class="section">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="reveal mb-12 text-center">
      <span class="badge">Food</span>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-4xl">
        Nearby Food &amp; Dining
      </h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-stone leading-relaxed">
        From local Ilocano empanada to casual cafes — here's where to eat near the windmills.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Must-Try Local -->
    <div class="reveal mx-auto mb-10 max-w-3xl rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-gold-light/20 to-gold-light/5 p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="text-4xl">🥟</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">Must Try: Ilocos Empanada</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone">The Iconic Street Food of Ilocos Norte</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-stone leading-relaxed">
        No trip to Bangui is complete without sampling the famous <strong>Ilocos
        Empanada</strong> — a deep-fried orange pastry stuffed with grated green papaya,
        longganisa (local sausage), and a whole egg. Vendors selling fresh empanada
        are often found near the central viewing area. Price: <strong>PHP 40–70</strong> each.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Restaurant Cards -->
    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <!-- 1. Kang Kang Windmill Cafe -->
      <div class="reveal card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">☕</span>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-navy">Kang Kang Windmill Cafe</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">
          A cozy café located right near the windmills, serving Filipino comfort food,
          coffee, and refreshments. The perfect spot to cool down after walking along
          the shoreline. Offers a view of the turbines from the dining area.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 2. Chingado BBQ -->
      <div class="reveal card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">🍖</span>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-navy">Chingado BBQ</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">
          Casual American-style BBQ joint offering grilled meats, burgers, and sides.
          A surprising find near the windmill area. Popular with both locals and tourists.
          Outdoor seating with a relaxed vibe.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3. 18 Degrees North Camping Cafe -->
      <div class="reveal card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">⛺</span>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-navy">18 Degrees North</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">
          A camping-style café and diner offering Filipino and Asian dishes. Known for
          its unique outdoor setting, Instagram-worthy presentation, and hearty meals.
          Serves breakfast, lunch, and dinner.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 4. Canton View Inn and Restaurant -->
      <div class="reveal card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">🏡</span>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-navy">Cañon View Inn & Restaurant</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">
          A family-friendly restaurant offering Filipino comfort food with views of the
          surrounding landscape. Good for larger groups. Located a short drive from the
          windmill area towards the Bangui town center.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 5. Bangui Town Eateries -->
      <div class="reveal card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">🍛</span>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-navy">Bangui Town Eateries</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">
          Several small carinderias (local eateries) in Bangui town proper, about 2–3 km
          from the windmills. Serving affordable Filipino dishes like adobo, sinigang,
          and grilled fish. Expect to pay <strong>PHP 80–150</strong> per meal.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 6. Souvenir Snacks -->
      <div class="reveal card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">🍦</span>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-navy">Souvenir & Snack Stalls</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">
          Small stalls near the central viewing area sell cold drinks, ice cream,
          chichacorn (Ilocos-style corn snacks), and souvenir items. Perfect for
          a quick refreshment while taking photos of the turbines.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
